AN ORDINANCE OF THE MAYOR AND COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF FOLKSTON, GEORGIA, PROHIBITING UNAUTHORIZED OVERNIGHT PARKING AND CAMPING ON CITY-OWNED OR CITY-CONTROLLED PROPERTY; PROVIDING DEFINITIONS; ESTABLISHING EXCEPTIONS; PROVIDING FOR ENFORCEMENT, REMOVAL OF VEHICLES, PENALTIES, SEVERABILITY, REPEALER, CODIFICATION, AND AN EFFECTIVE DATE; AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES.

WHEREAS, The Mayor and Council find that unauthorized overnight parking and camping on City property interferes with the intended public use of municipal facilities, creates health and safety concerns, increases maintenance costs, and exposes the City to unnecessary liability;

WHEREAS, The Mayor and Council further find that City-owned property is maintained for governmental and public purposes and should not be used for unauthorized residential occupancy or overnight lodging;

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ORDAINED by the Mayor and Council of the City of Folkston, Georgia, as follows:
